{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>I know not the day of my death.</b> Rabbi Yehoshua ben Karcha said: if a man reaches the age at which his forebears died, he should worry five years before and five years after. Yitzchak was 123 years old. He said: perhaps I am reaching the age of my mother — and she died at 127, and here I am within five years of her time. Therefore, <b>I know not the day of my death</b> — perhaps I am reaching my mother's time, perhaps my father's."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:00:42.081309332Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}